From a3f26b3c175dcd41c3e05f1915b70bf96cc03d1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivan Karpan <ivan.karpan@onereach.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:46:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] activation: Cooperate with Steam before detached game launch

Detached Wine games cannot inherit Steam's native activation context. Let the
foreground Steam client or helper yield activation to the game's bundle and
acknowledge the request before Wine starts. Inactive frontends decline and
expired requests cannot yield later; missing replies have a bounded wait.

Provide a native requester for Hadron's game route so compatibility queries
and installer helpers do not request activation. Keep spawn architecture and
environment handling unchanged.

Add isolated activation, routing-hook and process-lifecycle controls, including
delayed windows, deliberate switching, blocked callbacks and absent receivers.

Co-Authored-By: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
